# Digest 17: pattern 9, Classes, groups, other children, daycare as a place to grow

Share: baby-development/_work/2026-11/digests/share-17.md. Yes posts: 98. Near posts: 63.

All 161 supplied posts were read whole; none remain unread or were excluded. These are shares of one main pattern from the stated random sample of 20,000 posts, not estimates about all parents. Counts are posts, not quotes or people: apparent cross-posts retain their separate supplied post IDs, and repeated quote text within a post adds no count. Forms use “the parent” without inferring sex; unknown stages and speaker identities remain unknown. The near section also includes explicitly identified professional and other speakers.

Tags record explicit statements: tried means an action already taken toward the concern, including attending, seeking or arranging care/classes; a plan alone is no. Others means relevant actions or statements by other people, including caregivers and other children; mere attendance or the focal child’s behaviour alone is no. Bought requires an explicit completed purchase or payment, not an assumed fee for attendance; feeling requires the speaker to name a feeling. Per-post yes/no tags appear in Markdown comments below each Posts line.

## Pattern 9, share 17: yes posts

### The parent wants to prepare for a first separation and choose how gradually to start childcare.

7 of 98 posts.

Parents ask about short visits, staying alongside the child, half days versus full days, and changing feeding or sleep routines before care begins. Children range from a baby starting at five months to toddlers of 17–18 months; some have previously stayed only with parents or grandparents. One parent has already abandoned a YMCA attempt, while others have not yet begun separation.

- "How do we get this going? Do I bring her for a short period of time to begin with? Do I go and stay with her once or twice? Do I just rip the bandaid off and leave her there (that feels wrong)?" [sr072-0104]
- "My LO will be starting daycare at 5m. Wondering if people recommend doing half days the first week or if it’s easier on him to just get used to full days off the bat?" [sr038-0069]
- "[…] I tried to drop her at the YMCA childcare once, and I bailed after a few minutes because she was crying." [sr017-0045]
