6 of 63 posts.

Parents describe a toddler knocked down in an egg-hunt rush, being hit in a playroom, threats or rejection from older children, and conflict over toys. They want safer events, a response in the moment, self-advocacy or kinder inclusion; known focal ages are 18 months and two years, with others unknown. One parent of an autistic child asks for polite rejection rather than compulsory friendship, while another weighs competing advice about retaliation. Provenance: the playroom post’s author explicitly says Gemini helped draft the post and translate replies, adding thanks; its wording is AI-assisted, as disclosed in sr032-0051–0052.

- "[…] I blocked him as quick as I could and covered him as MORE KIDS hit me and acted like a human speed bump as I got hit over and over as he cried under me. […]" [sr004-0124]
