### The parent finds the child more clingy or wakeful at home after starting childcare.

3 of 98 posts.

Parents of children aged 18, almost 19 and 21 months describe new clinginess, tears or disturbed sleep after starting daycare or gym childcare. One child sees their mother at the same workplace during the day; another previously stayed with grandparents. The parents ask how to make the transition smoother and preserve sleep.

- "But since starting daycare he has become SO whiny. Every morning and every afternoon he whines constantly, wants to be carried all the time, and has meltdowns over the smallest things. […]" [sr035-0006]
- "[…] Since then, he has been really clingy at home and easily tearful whenever I leave the house which is a new behavior." [sr011-0204]
- "Sleep has been iffy now. Wakes and rolls and fusses till she falls asleep or we have to help. […]" [sr061-0105]
- "Did anyone else go through this? Did it pass? Any tips for helping with the transition without completely destroying his sleep habits?" [sr035-0008]

**But:** Distress at home can coexist with rapid settling at care: "[…] I know that when I drop him off crying he stops like 5 seconds after I leave." [sr035-0005] Illness is also a possible contributor in that post: "He also had a fever one day last week and now has some congestion, so I’m sure part of this is daycare germs too." [sr035-0007]

