### The parent wants meaningful nursery updates about the child’s care and development.

1 of 98 posts.

The parent of an almost-two-year-old says photos and staff knowledge have become less consistent in the older room. App logs and handover reports conflict, and the parent wants to hear about behaviour, learning and growth while both parents work. They have raised it informally and are considering a formal request.

- "[…] The app says she'll have eaten xyz then the person will say she didn't have much dinner today or vice versa. […]" [sr062-0117]
- "[…] It actually makes me feel quite sad knowing that she is doing so much of her learning and developing without us knowing anything about it because we both have to go to work. […]" [sr062-0118]
- "[…] I have mentioned it informally recently but tempted to make it more formal." [sr062-0118]

**But:** The parent still sees appealing activities in the photos that do arrive: "[…] when there are photos she seems to be doing the fun stuff that I'd want. […]" [sr062-0118]

