### The parent weighs starting group care for learning and company against keeping the child at home.

7 of 63 posts.

Parents weigh social learning, early friends, language, confidence and stimulation against separation, pressure or losing home time. Known children include just-two-year-olds and a 31-month-old; several ages are unknown, and two apparently cross-posted requests ask in advance about optional attendance. Constraints include full-day-only affordable options, long waitlists, family pressure about German exposure and uncertainty about the earliest benefit from Montessori.

