### The parent wants childcare that suits the child’s developmental needs and temperament.

9 of 63 posts.

Parents compare developmental attention, curriculum, consistent adults, child safety and classroom fit with convenience, cost or health risks. Known children range from three months to 22 months and two years; one nursery-tour child’s current age is unknown. Concerns include an infant alone in a container, repeated illness, a speech-delayed child’s routines or bleeding disorder, and a trusted childminder sharing a driveway with a man reported to have groomed young teenagers.

- "[…] an environment that prioritizes individual development while keeping them safe and happy vs one that will keep her safe and happy." [sr007-0038]
- "[…] She wasn’t crying and I have no idea how often that happens/how long she was in it, but I just felt kind of sad for her that she was by herself in a container […]" [sr013-0260]
- "A man (in his 40s) who lives very, very close by to my childminder (shared driveway) has been found grooming \*very young\* teenage girls. […]" [sr026-0077]
- "Does this sound like something a daycare would be able to manage? Is there any chance he could get extra supervision on play structures? […]" [sr098-0020]
- "Also should I mention she’s going in early development? Is this going to end up getting her kicked out?" [sr099-0134]
