- "[…] doing half days the first week […]" [sr038-0069]

**But:** A manager expects coping: "The daycare manager reassures me it’s all normal and fine and he will manage better that I expect. […]" [sr107-0012]

### The parent weighs group learning against staying home.

7 of 98 posts.

They consider readiness, social learning, illness and siblings.

- "[…] social and emotional skills with other peers her age. […]" [sr072-0085]
- "[…] bringing the sickness back to the new baby." [sr040-0056]

**But:** One former nanny questions the need: "[…] why put your child into a school like setting if you are able to teach them basic school skills […]" [sr027-0063]

### The parent questions baby swimming’s purpose and safety.

7 of 98 posts.

They ask about skills, comfort, equipment and instructor practices.

- "My baby's swimming instructor wants him to do a flip" [sr045-0001]
- "I guess I was expecting more water safety. […]" [sr011-0141]

**But:** Some pay for enjoyment: "It’s not really to teach him to swim, it’s to give him an activity to do, something fun for him […]" [sr013-0170]

### The parent doubts daycare gives enough comfort.

6 of 98 posts.

They question independence demands, brief soothing and pressure to sleep-train.

- "[…] "unseen" and distressed […]" [sr009-0099]
- "[…] they are also pushing me to sleep train, which i do not want to do." [sr017-0079]

**But:** Some report comfort: "They have been very patient and supportive and they do comfort her when she needs it […]" [sr091-0107]

### The parent worries peer contact is insufficient.

5 of 98 posts.

Work, transport and few parent friends restrict opportunities.

- "[…] he doesn’t have a ‘little bestie’. […]" [sr002-0140]
